  "answer": "I'll look through the storefront cart API and how store merchant settings are read so the quantity cap can be applied without a restart.The cap belongs on the storefront cart create and update paths, read from merchant configuration on each request so a change applies immediately.The storefront cart API now rejects a line quantity above the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` merchant setting (99 when that setting is absent). `POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi` read the value on each request and return HTTP 400 before any cart write, so the cart stays unchanged. A quantity of 0 still removes the line.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 responses and that the cart is left unchanged when a line exceeds the limit\", \"that a configuration change applies without a restart\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration test or fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and calls the cart create, update, and multi endpoints\"]}",
